{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.WenzlPochhammerBoundary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.WenzlPochhammerBoundary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.RootsOfUnity.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qInt_fourm_vanishes_at_zeta_fourm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qInt_fourm_vanishes_at_zeta_fourm","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WenzlPochhammerBoundary.lean#L47-L53","doc":"The Habiro-tower boundaries `[4m]_q = 0` at `ζ_{4m}` (the `[4]_q=0` /\n`[8]_q=0` / … annihilators): a primitive `4m`-th root of unity kills `[4m]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.qInt_root_vanishes_iff_dvd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.qInt_root_vanishes_iff_dvd","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WenzlPochhammerBoundary.lean#L34-L45","doc":"The quantum integer `[n]_q = (q^n − 1)/(q − 1)` vanishes at a primitive\n`m`-th root of unity `ζ` (with `m > 1`) exactly when `m ∣ n`. This is the\nWenzl–Pochhammer boundary structure: the roots of unity at which the Habiro\ntower truncates. ","signatureChunk":0}]}